00:00:54.954 --> 00:00:57.523
-From Rockefeller Center
in the heart of New York City,

00:00:57.523 --> 00:01:00.593
it's "The Tonight Show"
starring Jimmy Fallon.

00:01:00.593 --> 00:01:03.996
Tonight, join Jimmy
and his guests, Charlize Theron,

00:01:03.996 --> 00:01:05.765
Governor Andrew Cuomo,

00:01:05.765 --> 00:01:07.666
musical guest
Little Big Town,

00:01:07.666 --> 00:01:10.470
and featuring the legendary
Roots crew.

00:01:10.470 --> 00:01:14.273
And now,
here's your host, Jimmy Fallon.

00:01:14.273 --> 00:01:22.415 line:0%
♪♪

00:01:22.415 --> 00:01:30.556 line:0%
♪♪

00:01:30.556 --> 00:01:33.660
-Hi, everyone, and welcome to
"The Tonight Show."

00:01:33.660 --> 00:01:36.095
As you can see, we are back
in the studio

00:01:36.095 --> 00:01:39.131
at 30 Rockefeller Plaza
here in New York City.

00:01:39.131 --> 00:01:42.535
And as a New Yorker, I want to
say thank you to everyone

00:01:42.535 --> 00:01:44.804
who helped get us back to
where we are now,

00:01:44.804 --> 00:01:47.073
wearing masks,
social distancing,

00:01:47.073 --> 00:01:50.075
washing hands, quarantining,
it all helps.

00:01:50.075 --> 00:01:52.545
And to all the states going
through the tough parts

00:01:52.545 --> 00:01:55.147
right now, our friends
in Florida, Arizona,

00:01:55.147 --> 00:01:59.852
Texas, California, all over
the South, I know how hard it is

00:01:59.852 --> 00:02:02.955
and I'm not gonna lie to you --
it's rough.

00:02:02.955 --> 00:02:06.025
But I guess I'm here to show you
that there is a light

00:02:06.025 --> 00:02:08.360
at the end of the tunnel
if we all do our part

00:02:08.360 --> 00:02:10.830
to keep each other safe.

00:02:10.830 --> 00:02:14.734
I don't know if anyone else
feels this way, but normalcy,

00:02:14.734 --> 00:02:17.503
any type of normalcy
feels great.

00:02:17.503 --> 00:02:20.473
So hopefully we can put a smile
on your face for an hour

00:02:20.473 --> 00:02:22.508
every night and let you
sit back and relax

00:02:22.508 --> 00:02:25.912
while we try to bring you
just a little bit of normal.

00:02:25.912 --> 00:02:28.715
These are the hardest times
to do comedy,

00:02:28.715 --> 00:02:33.920
but they're also the times
when we need it the most.

00:02:33.920 --> 00:02:38.057
Maybe that's why comedy
was invented.

00:02:38.057 --> 00:02:41.060
Hmm.
-Hmm.

00:02:41.060 --> 00:02:45.899
-Chew on that.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:45.899 --> 00:02:48.167
As you're drifting off to sleep.

00:02:48.167 --> 00:02:49.768
[ Laughter ]

00:02:49.768 --> 00:02:54.841
Let that marinate for a bit
before you flip it on the grill.

00:02:54.841 --> 00:02:57.410
[ Laughter ]

00:02:57.410 --> 00:03:00.212
Either way, we here
at "The Tonight Show"

00:03:00.212 --> 00:03:02.648
always want to bring you
the best show possible.

00:03:02.648 --> 00:03:05.418
And that means having
the safest show possible.

00:03:05.418 --> 00:03:08.788
Everyone here in the studio
has tested negative for COVID

00:03:08.788 --> 00:03:12.025
and all of our crew are wearing
masks and face shields

00:03:12.025 --> 00:03:15.261
and we're all six feet apart.
Take a look.

00:03:15.261 --> 00:03:17.863
We are taking this
very seriously.

00:03:17.863 --> 00:03:20.899
And I want to thank NBC
for really doing a great job

00:03:20.899 --> 00:03:24.236
of making sure everyone here
feels safe.

00:03:24.236 --> 00:03:28.007
Just to walk you through my day,
when I got in this morning,

00:03:28.007 --> 00:03:31.977
I had a temperature check,
I did the nose swab test,

00:03:31.977 --> 00:03:35.047
the one that goes all the way
up into your brain.

00:03:35.047 --> 00:03:37.350
Yeah, I didn't know that
at the same time you can get

00:03:37.350 --> 00:03:43.055
a COVID test and a colonoscopy,
but, hey, we're learning, right?

00:03:43.055 --> 00:03:45.692
Anyway, once I was cleared,
I could go to my office

00:03:45.692 --> 00:03:47.092
and get ready for the show.

00:03:47.092 --> 00:03:50.096
In every part of the office
is a little slip of paper --

00:03:50.096 --> 00:03:53.132
thank you -- saying that
it's been disinfected.

00:03:53.132 --> 00:03:54.366
Yeah.

00:03:54.366 --> 00:03:57.770
This was truly done
the safety way possible.

00:03:57.770 --> 00:03:59.105
Thank you.

00:03:59.105 --> 00:04:01.474
And we would only do it that way

00:04:01.474 --> 00:04:03.943
if that was the case,
the safety way.

00:04:03.943 --> 00:04:07.112
We're thankful to have
the Roots with us tonight.

00:04:07.112 --> 00:04:09.849
I'm very happy to see you guys.

00:04:09.849 --> 00:04:11.984
I missed you.

00:04:11.984 --> 00:04:13.720
Sent a bunch of texts.

00:04:13.720 --> 00:04:16.088
[ Laughter ]

00:04:16.088 --> 00:04:18.057
Didn't hear back.

00:04:18.057 --> 00:04:21.027
[ Laughter ]

00:04:21.027 --> 00:04:22.961
The show is gonna be
a little different

00:04:22.961 --> 00:04:24.162
than what you're used to.

00:04:24.162 --> 00:04:25.264
There is no audience.

00:04:25.264 --> 00:04:26.966
The guests will be
streaming from home.

00:04:26.966 --> 00:04:28.801
But I think in some ways

00:04:28.801 --> 00:04:30.569
we're all kind of
getting used to different.

00:04:30.569 --> 00:04:32.705
But what we want you to know
is that we are here for you

00:04:32.705 --> 00:04:35.474
and we are slowly and safely
getting back to work

00:04:35.474 --> 00:04:37.644
and back to whatever normal is.

00:04:37.644 --> 00:04:40.913
So welcome again to "The Tonight
Show" and thanks for watching.

